   **Description:** The `collectFees` function iterates over the entire balance of the `feeCollector` contract using `feeCollector.balanceOf(address(this))`. If the `feeCollector` contract holds a large number of tokens, the loop can become unbounded, leading to a denial of service condition where the function call runs out of gas.

   **Impact:** The `collectFees` function could become unusable if the `feeCollector` contract accumulates a large balance, preventing the collection of fees.

   **Mitigation:**  
   ```solidity
   // Limit the number of tokens processed in a single transaction
   function collectFees(address payable collector) public virtual {
       require(msg.sender == feeCollector, "Only fee collector can collect");
       uint256 maxTokens = 1000; // Limit the number of tokens processed
       uint256 totalFees = 0;
       for (uint i = 0; i < maxTokens && feeCollector.balanceOf(address(this)) > 0; i++) {
           totalFees = totalFees.add(fees[address(this)][i]);
       }
       require(totalFees > 0, "No fees to collect");
       feeCollector.transfer(totalFees);
       emit FeeCollected(feeCollector, totalFees);
   }
   ```

