   **Description:**  
   The `mint` function allows the owner to mint tokens to any address, including potentially themselves, without any restrictions or checks. This can lead to centralization issues and potential abuse.

   **Impact:**  
   The owner can mint tokens to themselves or to any other address they choose, leading to potential abuse and centralization of token supply.

   **Mitigation:**  
   ```solidity
   function mint(address to, uint256 amount) public onlyOwner {
        require(to != address(0), "Minting to the zero address.");
       require(totalSupply() + amount <= _maxSupply, "Minting would exceed max supply.");
       _mint(to, amount);
   }
